Cached the base-type lookup and replaced the byte-by-byte shift loop with a size switch using unaligned `memcpy` loads for the common 1/2/4/8-byte cases, keeping the original loop only as a fallback. This removes repeated `GetType()` calls and loop overhead while preserving the exact result.

```include
